From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 01:43:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 135/160] fix: ccam sun-shafts-off did nothing - the stage gate
 never read SunShafts_Active; add a renderer-side suppress flag

Root cause: 92a2236c pinned the Time of Day's `SunShafts_Active` to 0 on the
post-effect bus. Nothing in the 5.7 pipeline reads that parameter.
`CSunShaftsStage::IsStageActive` is `r_sunshafts && r_PostProcess` only, and
every consumer (the half-res downsample decision, Execute, the tone map's
featureMask / texture bind) goes through it. The old `CSunShafts::Preprocess`
that ANDed the param with the cvar is not even defined in this tree; the TOD's
visibility sliders act through SunShafts_Amount / RaysAmount. The apply did run
(editor.log has the `sun shafts off` line twice) - it just wrote a value with no
reader. Ordering vs SyncMainWithRender, bForceValue and the editor path are
all irrelevant.

Fix (the trodden path - a bus request the renderer ANDs, like every other
Global_User_ camera param):
- CPostEffectsMgr: new `Global_User_SunShaftsSuppressed` (no-transition
  float, default 0).
- CSunShaftsStage::IsStageActive: cvars AND NOT flag. Flag 0 = byte-identical.
- ccam ApplySunShaftsOff/RestoreSunShafts publish 1 / 0 on that flag instead of
  touching the TOD's param; m_savedSunShaftsActive removed; per-frame
  re-assert and the once-per-activation log kept.
- Docs (README, SceneReferredContent, ConsoleReference) corrected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
